Carmen spent 10 minutes per crossword puzzle and solved 3 crossword puzzles, so she spent 10 * 3 = 30 minutes on crossword puzzles.

Carmen spent 5 minutes per sudoku puzzle and solved 8 sudoku puzzles, so she spent 5 * 8 = 40 minutes on sudoku puzzles.

In total, Carmen spent 30 + 40 = 70 minutes playing these games.

So, the final answer is 70.

\boxed{70}
2-9034 \boxed{410}

Let the time it takes Carmen to finish a crossword puzzle be $t_c = 10$ minutes.
Let the time it takes Carmen to finish a sudoku puzzle be $t_s = 5$ minutes.
Carmen solved 3 crossword puzzles, so the total time spent on crossword puzzles is $3 \times t_c = 3 \times 10 = 30$ minutes.
Carmen solved 8 sudoku puzzles, so the total time spent on sudoku puzzles is $8 \times t_s = 8 \times 5 = 40$ minutes.
The total time Carmen spent playing these games is the sum of the time spent on crossword puzzles and the time spent on sudoku puzzles: $30 + 40 = 70$ minutes.

\boxed{70}

